# New feature git setup

Before writing code for a new feature:

1. `git fetch origin`
2. `git checkout main` and `git pull origin main`
3. `git checkout -b feat/<short-slug>` from that updated `main`
4. Call `SetActiveBranch` with the new branch name

Never start feature work on `main` or on an unrelated feature branch. If the working tree is dirty, stop and ask before switching.

Branch names: `feat/<slug>` for features, `fix/<slug>` for bug fixes. Keep the slug short and concrete (`feat/react-router`, not `feat/update-stuff`).
